<title>FRANCE: U.S. dominates Paris June air cargo imports.</title>
<headline>U.S. dominates Paris June air cargo imports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S was the principal country of origin for import traffic handled at the Paris airports in June 1997, Aeroports de Paris (ADP),said.</p>
<p>June 1997 import traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 42,941 tonnes, an increase of 4.1 percent on the same period last year, Aeroports de Paris.</p>
<p>The 20 countries of origin for ADP imports in June 1997 with percentage change on June 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>     Origin		tonnes	Percent</p>
<p>					     Change 1996</p>
<p>     1. United States   12,360  down  7.1</p>
<p>     2. Canada	     2,363    up  8.9</p>
<p>     3. UK		   2,204    up 94.9</p>
<p>     4. Japan		2,181    up 21.7</p>
<p>     5. Hong Kong	  1,651    up 23.7</p>
<p>     6. Germany	    1,527    up 14.3</p>
<p>     7. India		1,516  down 32.7</p>
<p>     8. Thailand	   1,186    up 32.4</p>
<p>     9. Italy		1,086  down  2.8</p>
<p>    10. Singapore	    599    up 91.4</p>
<p>    11. China		  583    up 89.4</p>
<p>    12. Brazil		 577  down  0.9</p>
<p>    13. U.A.E.		 558    up  5.2</p>
<p>    14. Kenya		  542  down 34.7</p>
<p>    15. Senegal		533  down  9.7</p>
<p>    16. Taiwan		 519    up 48.9</p>
<p>    17. Sweden		 472  down  2.5</p>
<p>    18. Fr. West Indies    453    up 20.3</p>
<p>    19. South Africa	 445  down 21.5</p>
<p>    20. Argentina	    432    up 10.2</p>
